-- KNOWN GAP, not a discovery: check::check_module's own doc comment
-- already names this narrow gap (inherited from Fix #10, never
-- introduced by it): build_instance_table's coherence pass only sees a
-- module's own declared instances -- prelude::seed's builtin table is
-- only merged in afterward (InstanceTable::merge_from, which silently
-- keeps whichever side is `self`, no diagnostic either way). Re-declaring
-- Eq on a type that already has a builtin Eq instance -- Int, here --
-- neither reports DuplicateInstance nor is rejected any other way. See
-- checker_impl_summary.md's own "Known gaps" section. Expected once
-- fixed: a DuplicateInstance error at this declaration's own span.
instance Eq Int where
  (==) a b = False
